#clinical-finding(title: [Molecular Evidence That ME/CFS Fatigue Is Distinct from Other Fatigue States])[
An exploratory extracellular-vesicle (EV) microRNA (miRNA) analysis distinguished ME/CFS from both idiopathic chronic fatigue and depression with a 62-miRNA signature achieving 87% sensitivity and 94% specificity @Eguchi2026EVmiRNAfatigue. ME/CFS-derived EVs also showed a unique size and fluorescence profile, and key miRNAs (miR-21-5p, let-7f-5p, miR-26b-5p, miR-20a-5p) differed between groups.

(Certainty: 0.50, very small discovery cohort, n=6 per group; discounted 0.50. Preliminary — requires replication.)

*Limitations:* Tiny exploratory sample (n=6 ME/CFS); no independent validation; early-stage marker, far from a clinical test.

*Reputation:* Not yet replicated; discovery findings of this size are high-risk for non-reproducibility.

*Severity applicability:* Unknown — discovery cohort not stratified by severity.

*Consequence:* If confirmed, a blood-based molecular signal could eventually help distinguish ME/CFS fatigue from the fatigue of depression or idiopathic chronic fatigue — conditions that appear similar to an observer but may need different care. This is early and may prove to be a dead end.
] <clf:fatigue-differentiation-biomarker>
